cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below, and cite the JuniperMapper dataset and paper it builds on."
title: "shrubs-segmentation"
abstract: >-
  Instance segmentation-based approach to shrub delineation. It studies how
  transfer learning and deep learning models (Matterport Mask R-CNN,
  Detectron2 Mask R-CNN and SAM 3) trained on the JuniperMapper dataset can
  segment shrubs in a burnt area near Encinacorba (Spain).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Iranzo
    given-names: Cristian
    email: c.iranzo@unizar.es
repository-code: "https://github.com/CristianICS/shrubs-segmentation"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - shrub delineation
  - instance segmentation
  - Mask R-CNN
  - Detectron2
  - SAM 3
  - LiDAR
  - remote sensing
